        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This should now [be fixed on latest `main`](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/6a8aab4b07c6caa1d0643c1c9dccd5b2d5f5e094/lua/mini/base16.lua#L1342-L1369) (along with parallel integration in 'mini.hues'). I manually tested the final groups and not all of them needed to be set. And setting all `XxxKind` groups indeed is what a good color scheme should be doing (although 'blink.cmp' itself can be a bit more flexible here by reusing highlights from 'mini.icons').\r\n\r\nThanks again for the PR! I've added you as a co-author of the 'mini.base16' integration commit.",
